title: "Iniciar sesión — Área de Miembros"
---
{#- All three login pages POST to the SAME endpoint, /members/login. The page a
    person lands on only decides which language they read and where an error
    sends them back to — it does not decide which members area they end up in.
    That is resolved server-side from the token's own preferred_language
    (auth_service/app.py), which is the only thing that actually knows. -#}
<div class="login-card">
  <h1>Área de Miembros</h1>
  <p class="sub">Ingresá la contraseña que recibiste por email al suscribirte a All-Access.</p>

  <div class="error" id="login-error">Contraseña incorrecta. Intentá de nuevo.</div>

  <form method="POST" action="/members/login" id="login-form">
    <label for="password">Contraseña</label>
    <input type="password" id="password" name="password" required autocomplete="current-password">
    {#- Empty on purpose. A hardcoded "/members/" here would override the
        language routing for every subscriber in every language. It is filled in
        by the script below only when Caddy actually gated a specific page. -#}
    <input type="hidden" name="next" id="next-field" value="">
    <input type="hidden" name="lang" value="es">
    <button type="submit">Ingresar</button>
  </form>

  <p class="help"><a href="/members/forgot-password">¿Olvidaste tu contraseña?</a></p>
  <p class="help">¿Problemas para ingresar? Escribinos a <a href="mailto:coach@triaperformance.com">coach@triaperformance.com</a></p>

  <p class="auth-lang">
    <a href="/members/login" class="current">Español</a><span class="sep">·</span><a href="/members/en/login">English</a><span class="sep">·</span><a href="/members/pt/login">Português</a>
  </p>
</div>

<script>
  // Show the error banner if redirected back with ?error=1
  if (new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('error') === '1') {
    document.getElementById('login-error').classList.add('show');
  }
  // Preserve where the visitor was trying to go before being gated, if present.
  // Only same-site absolute paths are accepted: `next` arrives from the query
  // string, so anything else is an open-redirect waiting to be found.
  var next = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('next');
  if (next && /^\/[^/\\]/.test(next)) document.getElementById('next-field').value = next;
</script>
